atrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n\nIII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186433173 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433173 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+5{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186447724 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447724 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447724 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447725 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447725 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447725 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f54d7916-c701-5bcb-a279-b7f11eb4abc1" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447726 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447726 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447726 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ffcee29-8511-5be3-b402-b9d385d893a3" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447727 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447727 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447727 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e6f44350-5bbe-53da-b5c6-334f8d6ab627" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447728 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447728 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447728 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "079cb409-a3a7-51e0-b8f0-ea41f4f0d754" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447729 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447729 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186447729 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "039313ab-026d-502b-abed-f28f52722a46" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186447724 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186447725 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448902 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448902 #edb/ref 1077 "I" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186448902 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 1